      "title": "Trump administration again denies entry visas to Palestinian officials ahead of UN general assembly",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/17/trump-denies-visas-palestine-un",
      "description": "<p>For the second year in a row, the administration has barred the Palestinian delegation from US travel for the forum</p><p>The US state department said on Wednesday that it had again denied entry visas to Palestinian officials ahead next week’s <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/unitednations\">United Nations</a> general assembly gathering in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york\">New York</a>.</p><p>The state department said in a <a href=\"https://www.state.gov/releases/office-of-the-spokesman/2026/09/sanctioning-officials-of-the-palestinian-authority-and-members-of-the-palestine-liberation-organization-2/\">statement</a> the Palestinian Authority (PA) and the Palestine Liberation Organization (PLO) had “failed to live up to their commitments”, accusing the groups of “taking actions to internationalize the Israeli-Palestinian Conflict including through the International Criminal Court (ICC) and International Court of Justice (ICJ)” and of “glorifying terrorism” among other allegations.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/17/trump-denies-visas-palestine-un\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-18T00:42:39"
    },
    {
      "title": "State Department Extends Visa Ban on Abbas, Other Palestinian Officials",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/16/us/politics/visa-ban-abbas.html",
      "description": "The move would prevent Mahmoud Abbas, the leader of two governing Palestinian groups, from traveling to the United States next week for the United Nations General Assembly.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-09-17T09:24:20"
    }
